{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791691251,"nonce":"3c/uulMkH9NKMioe0qxeDQ+NbsA=","title":"Concurrent startup migrations race (two processes migrating at once)","message":"From the C6 check: two consoles started at the same moment on a fresh DB both ran migrate(); the second failed with 'migration 0022_fit_score_decisions failed: duplicate column name: evidence_mode' after taking a pre-migrate backup mid-way through the first one's run. migrate() is not serialized across processes. Realistic on the host when a console restart coincides with a timer job or CLI command after a merge. Fix: take an exclusive migration lock (flock on \u003cdb\u003e.migrate.lock, or BEGIN IMMEDIATE around the version check + apply loop with a re-check of pending migrations after acquiring) so a second process waits and then finds nothing pending. Relates to C12 (ef185ba).","files":null}]}